    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and the full `mvn test` build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added the \"reject duplicate normalized telephone \u2192 409\" rule to `POST /api/owners` as a new, self-contained pipeline step, keeping structural impact low \u2014 no existing function bodies were modified, only one YAML line rewired.\n\n**New files (each a small, single-method unit):**\n- `EnsureUniqueOwnerTelephone.java` \u2014 after normalization, scans owners via `ownerRepository.findAll()`, comparing digit-normalized telephones (excluding the owner itself by id), and throws a checked `DuplicateTelephoneException` on a match.\n- `DuplicateTelephoneException.java` \u2014 checked exception.\n- `DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` with a `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the existing `InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler`.\n- `...escalation/...DuplicateTelephoneException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Edit:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted an `ensureUniqueTelephone` step (under `govern: [ transaction ]`) between `normalizeTelephone` and `save`.\n\nRunning after normalization means the check compares fully normalized 10-digit values, and it re-normalizes each stored telephone so seed data in any format is compared consistently. Both new acceptance tests (`coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone`, `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone`) and the full suite pass.",
